<title>UK: London tea auction sees encore for landed types.</title>
<headline>London tea auction sees encore for landed types.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Monday's London tea auction saw better liquoring Assams hold their values from Thursday's auction while plainer types eased again, the official report said.</p>
<p>East Africans tended firm with coloury descriptions posting the biggest increases in good overall demand.</p>
<p>Offshore teas met with good competition, securing firmer rates.</p>
<p>The next auction will be on Monday, December 2nd.</p>
<p>-London Newsroom, +44 171 542 8071</p>
